{
  "id": "Compound::DB01192 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Oxymorphone is linked to Cyp3a4 through a series of molecular and pharmacological pathways that converge on the opioid receptor agonist category. The evidence suggests that Oxymorphone, as an opioid agonist, is included in the broader class of full opioid agonists, which in turn bind to Cyp3a4. This indicates a potential mechanism where Oxymorphone, through its pharmacological properties, influences the expression or activity of Cyp3a4, likely via the opioid receptor pathway. The presence of multiple pathways, including those involving Sufentanil and Alfentanil, further supports a common mechanism where opioid agonists interact with Cyp3a4, possibly through shared receptor or metabolic pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of opioid receptor agonists in modulating Cyp3a4 activity, underscoring the importance of the opioid receptor in drug metabolism.",
